<https://www.ammitto.org/entity/ch/5072>
  a ammitto:PersonEntity ;
  ammitto:entityType "person" ;
  ammitto:hasName [ a ammitto:NameVariant ; ammitto:fullName "Kazak Viktar Uladzimiravich" ; ammitto:isPrimary "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
  ammitto:hasSanctionEntry <https://www.ammitto.org/entry/ch/consolidated-list/5072> ;
  ammitto:remarks "Judge at the Moskovski Rayon Court of the city of Minsk. He was directly involved in the judicial repression of the peaceful demonstrators on 19 Dec 2010. On 20 Dec 2010, he sentenced civil society activists Siarhei Arlou and Dzmitry Kresik to 12 days in jail, and Valeria Niadzvitskaya, Valiantsyna Busko and Hanna Dainiak to 10 days in jail. On 27 Dec 2010, he sentenced the deputy leader of the \"Young Front\" to 10 days in jail for his participation in the demonstration on 19 Dec 2010. On 4 and 7 Jul 2011, on 8 Nov 2011, and on 20 Dec 2011, he sentenced several activists (Viktoriya Bandarenka, 10 days in jail; Andrei Zakhareuski, 5 days in jail; Mikhail Muski, 7 days in jail; Raman Grytsevich, 7 days in jail). The way he conducted the trials was a clear violation of the Code of Criminal Procedure. He sustained the use of evidence and testimonies irrelevant to the accused." .
