<https://www.ammitto.org/entity/ch/69636>
  a ammitto:OrganizationEntity ;
  ammitto:entityType "organization" ;
  ammitto:hasName [ a ammitto:NameVariant ; ammitto:fullName "Lebedev Institute of Precision Mechanics and Computer Engineering" ; ammitto:isPrimary "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
  ammitto:hasSanctionEntry <https://www.ammitto.org/entry/ch/consolidated-list/69636> ;
  ammitto:remarks "The Lebedev Institute of Precision Mechanics and Computer Engineering is an entity that operates in the Russian IT sector, including in the field of computer and semiconductor development. The Lebedev Institute of Precision Mechanics and Computer Engineering is owned by the Russian Federation. The shareholder rights are exercised by the Federal Property Management Agency. The Lebedev Institute of Precision Mechanics and Computer Engineering holds a licence administered by the Russian Ministry of Industry and trade, as well as a licence administered by the Federal Security Service of the Russian Federation (FSB). The licence administered by the Russian Ministry of Industry and Trade covers the “development, production, testing, installation, maintenance, disposal and sale of weapons and military equipment”. The FSB licence is issued to IT companies that develop encryption and cryptography technology, information systems and telecommunication systems for the Russian intelligence services, as well as IT companies that develop personal database management systems for the Russian security services (i.e. tools specifically designed to store, retrieve, and manage large amounts of data obtained through, for example, social media scraping or other intelligence gathering practices)." .
