<https://www.ammitto.org/entity/ch/95492>
  a ammitto:OrganizationEntity ;
  ammitto:entityType "organization" ;
  ammitto:hasName [ a ammitto:NameVariant ; ammitto:fullName "Zhu Jiang Shipmanagement Co., Ltd" ; ammitto:isPrimary "true"^^xsd:boolean ] ;
  ammitto:hasSanctionEntry <https://www.ammitto.org/entry/ch/consolidated-list/95492> ;
  ammitto:remarks "Zhu Jiang Shipmanagement Co., Ltd is a company registered in Hong Kong and is the technical manager of crude oil tanker ARGENT (formerly JAGUAR, IMO: 9293002). ARGENT is not registered with the International Group of Protection and Indemnity Clubs and therefore is sailing without a trusted liability cover. It is also the only vessel managed by Zhu Jiang Shipmanagement Co., Ltd, which indicates that it operates under a non-transparent corporate governance policy. ARGENT has changed management companies and flag state multiple times in the last few years and has also sailed without a flag. It has also not verified its Automatic Identification Systems on multiple occasions. ARGENT is a vessel that has transported crude oil or petroleum products, originating in Russia or exported from Russia, while practicing irregular and high-risk shipping practices as set out in the International Maritime Organisation General Assembly resolution A.1192(33). As the technical manager of the tanker, Zhu Jiang Shipmanagement Co., Ltd is therefore managing and operating a vessel that transports crude oil or petroleum products, originating in Russia or exported from Russia, while practicing irregular and high-risk shipping practices as set out in the International Maritime Organisation General Assembly resolution A.1192(33)." .
